course: dictionary
lesson: 14181
title: Words about money
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Monetary means to do with money, especially the money used in a country. «The old coin is worth only two pounds, so its monetary value is small.» Monetary value means how much something is worth in money.
explain: Look at the words around the new word. The sentence talks about pounds and worth, so the clue points to money. Try your meaning in the sentence: «its money value is small» still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: You will meet monetary in maths and in news about banks. «The school sold cakes to raise money, then counted the monetary total at the end.» The total is an amount of money, so monetary is about money.
fact: Monetary means to do with money.
fact: «Monetary value» means how much something is worth in money.
fact: «Monetary unit» means a unit of money, such as a pound.
fact: «Monetary policy» is what a central bank does with money and interest.
fact: Monetary comes from money, so the word always points you back to money.
exercise: «The old coin is worth only two pounds, so its monetary value is small.» What does monetary value mean? | How old it is | What country it came from | *How much it is worth in money | How heavy it is
exercise: «Work out the monetary value of three coins, each worth 20p.» What do you need to find? | *How much money the three coins are worth together | How many coins are in a bag | What colour the coins are | How old the coins are
exercise: «The bank changed its monetary policy this year.» What does this sentence tell you? | The bank held a party for its customers | The bank closed for a holiday | The bank painted its walls | *The bank changed how it handles money and interest
test: «The prize was a gift card, so its monetary value was ten pounds.» What is the monetary value of the prize? | Very exciting | A gift card | Ten prizes | *Ten pounds
test: Ben says monetary means to do with the weather. Is he right? | Yes, it means to do with plants | No, it means to do with food | Yes, it means to do with the weather | *No, monetary means to do with money
exam: Which of these is a monetary unit? | A litre | *A pound | A metre | A kilogram
